# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.{api,worker,tenant-console,platform-admin}: the
# repository root. Dependencies and build output are produced inside the builder
# stage, so host copies are never sent. Everything the builder copies stays
# included — package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, turbo.json,
# apps/ and packages/ sources — as does the Markdown under packages/second-brain
# that the knowledge loader reads at runtime. The host npm configuration is
# deliberately excluded; builds use only public lockfile dependencies.

# Secrets and VCS metadata
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.git
.github

# Installed dependencies and build output (recreated by pnpm install and the builds)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo

# Test, coverage, and tooling output
coverage
**/coverage
logs
**/*.log

# Documents and planning material: no image reads these
docs
plans
scratch
testcases
implement
